From: YSPEED firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] spi: mt7621: accept SPI_NO_CS for a GPIO-driven panel chip select

The YS-GPS-12832 panel chip select is driven from userspace on GPIO6, so the
spidev device asks for SPI_NO_CS. The SPI core rejects any mode bit the
controller does not advertise, so the capability has to be declared here.

The controller's native chip-select callback still runs for this device: in
spi_set_cs(), SPI_NO_CS is honoured only on the GPIO-chip-select path. That is
harmless because the CS1 pad is muxed to GPIO, so the controller's CS output
does not reach the panel.

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-mt7621.c
@@ -323 +323 @@ static int mt7621_spi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
-	host->mode_bits = SPI_LSB_FIRST;
+	host->mode_bits = SPI_LSB_FIRST | SPI_NO_CS;
